## v3.7.0 (2026-08-03)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2255 / PR #2598 automation-loop review and merge.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Added the scanner-remediation trigger and required a current-head fix plus regression
  coverage before a review can return GO.
- Recorded PR #2598's first-head NOGO, follow-up exact-head review, exclusive GO-label
  transition, required-check completion, and conditional merge.

### Why

PR #2598 showed that a superficially related docstring/test-expectation change can leave a
scanner-backed issue completely unresolved. The loop correctly kept the first head at NOGO;
the next head added a regression for retired scanner inputs, after which the matching review
authorized GO and `merge_wait` merged only that reviewed head. The independent required checks
completed the repository merge contract but did not authorize review.

