## v3.3.0 (2026-08-03)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2385 / PR #2570 automation-loop review and merge.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Added a multi-cycle audit rule: match the authorizing review's `commit_id` to the final PR head;
  reviews of superseded heads are historical evidence only.
- Clarified that review state and body content do not authorize advancement; the exact-head review,
  exclusive GO/NOGO label transition, required-check completion, and merge are separate facts.
- Recorded PR #2570's final-head review and NOGO-to-GO-to-required-checks-to-merge ordering.

### Why

PR #2570 accumulated five review records across three heads. The final path was trustworthy only
after the review bound to `219ec8ce`, followed by the loop-owned GO transition and a merge after
required checks completed. Reading the latest review prose or any prior review as transferable
authorization would have approved a superseded revision.

