## v3.0.0 (2026-07-28)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2233 / PR #2345 automation-loop review and merge.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Added unresolved automation-created review threads as a fail-closed stand-down condition.
- Recorded that repeated runs against unchanged unresolved thread state are not progress.
- Captured the successful continuation: all 12 threads resolved, fresh review of exact head
  `c6c59048` returned GO, labels transitioned exclusively, and the reviewed head merged.
- Replaced the temporary stand-by-only merge guidance with the active contract:
  `merge_wait` revalidates the process-local proof and conditionally squash-merges only the
  exact reviewed head without arming native auto-merge.

### Why

PR #2345 demonstrated the complete thread-aware review-to-merge path. The loop correctly
retained NOGO while it could not safely resolve automation-created threads. Once every thread
had a concrete resolution, a fresh exact-head review—not the prior audit prose—authorized the
GO label. The reviewed head then merged after required checks passed, proving the normal
conditional merge continuation that supersedes the temporary stand-by-only interlock.

